  "question": {
    "text": "As shown in the following figures, block of mass <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is in equilibrium in the vertical plane.<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0062_5d8324d9c06c.jpg\" /><br />\r<br />\rAt a certain instant right spring in case-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> and right string in case-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> are cut. Then the ratio of instantaneous acceleration of block in case-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> to case-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> just after the cutting is (strings and springs are ideal)"
  },
